p8GQ.png" alt=3D"Process of the algorithm (Image by Author)" class=3D"wp-im=
age-594206 not-transparent"><figcaption class=3D"wp-element-caption">Proces=
s of the algorithm (Image by Author)</figcaption></figure>
<h2 class=3D"wp-block-heading">Math</h2>
<p class=3D"wp-block-paragraph">In this section, we are learning a more gen=
eralized algorithm by looking at its math details. Here is the whole algori=
thm in math formulas.</p>
<figure class=3D"wp-block-image size-large"><img data-dominant-color=3D"f3f=
4f6" data-has-transparency=3D"true" style=3D"--dominant-color: #f3f4f6;" lo=
ading=3D"lazy" decoding=3D"async" width=3D"1296" height=3D"958" src=3D"http=
s://towardsdatascience.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/01/1dIHrPFBT2fmXuTXMb-3_=
Xw.png" alt=3D"Source: adapted from Wikipedia and Friedman's paper" class=
=3D"wp-image-593697 has-transparency"><figcaption class=3D"wp-element-capti=
on">Source: adapted from <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gradient_=
boosting">Wikipedia</a> and <a href=3D"https://jerryfriedman.su.domains/ftp=
/trebst.pdf">Friedman=E2=80=99s paper</a></figcaption></figure>
<p class=3D"wp-block-paragraph">Let=E2=80=99s take a close look at it line =
by line.</p>
<h3 class=3D"wp-block-heading">Step 1</h3>
<figure class=3D"wp-block-image size-large"><img data-dominant-color=3D"f4f=
5f8" data-has-transparency=3D"true" style=3D"--dominant-color: #f4f5f8;" lo=
ading=3D"lazy" decoding=3D"async" width=3D"800" height=3D"104" src=3D"https=
